WEBVTT

NOTE
Journey: Advocates — Week 23 Leader Video
Unit 6, Lesson 3: Prophecy

1
00:00:06.860 --> 00:00:09.260
All right, prophecy.

2
00:00:09.260 --> 00:00:11.220
Now think of it this way.

3
00:00:11.220 --> 00:00:16.220
If the Bible is both accurate and trustworthy,

4
00:00:16.860 --> 00:00:19.460
and we can know it to be true,

5
00:00:19.460 --> 00:00:22.940
or we can also know it to be historical,

6
00:00:22.940 --> 00:00:26.640
what then does that say about prophecy?

7
00:00:27.620 --> 00:00:29.060
Prophecy is tricky.

8
00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:32.380
It's almost like we can believe

9
00:00:32.380 --> 00:00:35.300
that the Bible is accurate history.

10
00:00:35.420 --> 00:00:37.940
We can show that and it's concrete

11
00:00:37.940 --> 00:00:41.180
and it kind of aligns up with some other things.

12
00:00:41.180 --> 00:00:44.540
And we can show that the Bible is completely accurate

13
00:00:44.540 --> 00:00:45.860
across all of history,

14
00:00:45.860 --> 00:00:49.060
and that 95% the same exact thing

15
00:00:49.060 --> 00:00:53.100
that what Jesus actually said or whatever.

16
00:00:54.380 --> 00:00:56.860
Prophecy is trickier

17
00:00:56.860 --> 00:00:59.500
because prophecy can be something

18
00:00:59.500 --> 00:01:01.380
that you might just discount and go,

19
00:01:01.380 --> 00:01:03.780
well, that just sort of was the happenstance

20
00:01:03.780 --> 00:01:05.100
or just coincidence.

21
00:01:05.100 --> 00:01:07.420
And it just sort of happened that way

22
00:01:07.420 --> 00:01:10.860
or maybe it was manufactured to look like

23
00:01:10.860 --> 00:01:12.740
it was fulfillment of prophecy.

24
00:01:14.220 --> 00:01:17.100
So here's the deal with this week.

25
00:01:17.100 --> 00:01:20.180
As you go through piece by piece,

26
00:01:20.180 --> 00:01:23.020
as you walk students through the misconceptions

27
00:01:23.020 --> 00:01:24.020
and the illuminations,

28
00:01:24.020 --> 00:01:26.060
as you walk your students through

29
00:01:26.060 --> 00:01:27.620
and help guide them

30
00:01:27.620 --> 00:01:30.060
through their introduction activity

31
00:01:30.060 --> 00:01:35.060
and exploration of Isaiah chapter 52 and 53.

32
00:01:35.220 --> 00:01:37.860
As you look at the questions

33
00:01:37.860 --> 00:01:40.020
and you start to piece this whole week together,

34
00:01:40.020 --> 00:01:43.700
I want you to keep one thing in mind this week

35
00:01:43.700 --> 00:01:44.540
and that's it.

36
00:01:45.620 --> 00:01:48.180
This week could be a difficult week.

37
00:01:49.020 --> 00:01:51.540
This could be the week, one of those weeks

38
00:01:51.540 --> 00:01:55.020
that students start firing all kinds of questions at you,

39
00:01:56.300 --> 00:01:59.140
especially your small group leaders.

40
00:01:59.140 --> 00:02:01.220
So here's what we're gonna do.

41
00:02:02.220 --> 00:02:04.660
We're gonna write the questions down

42
00:02:04.660 --> 00:02:07.220
and we're gonna dig in and do some research.

43
00:02:07.220 --> 00:02:09.940
And I want you to come back if you have to

44
00:02:09.940 --> 00:02:14.940
even take an addition week to answer those questions.

45
00:02:15.580 --> 00:02:17.660
Don't pretend like you have all the answers.

46
00:02:17.660 --> 00:02:19.380
Now you might have a bunch of the answers

47
00:02:19.380 --> 00:02:20.460
and that's awesome.

48
00:02:20.460 --> 00:02:22.060
But if you don't,

49
00:02:22.060 --> 00:02:24.460
don't pretend and don't brush it off

50
00:02:24.460 --> 00:02:26.260
because we're sort of at that moment now

51
00:02:26.260 --> 00:02:28.900
where you probably have students that are like,

52
00:02:29.340 --> 00:02:32.220
especially if they started very skeptical,

53
00:02:32.220 --> 00:02:35.140
hopefully they're walking closer and closer

54
00:02:35.140 --> 00:02:37.380
and closer and closer.

55
00:02:37.380 --> 00:02:39.940
But the closer you get,

56
00:02:39.940 --> 00:02:42.580
the easier it is to just fall off the edge

57
00:02:43.500 --> 00:02:45.860
because if we discount a question,

58
00:02:47.060 --> 00:02:48.620
the train may just come off the rails

59
00:02:48.620 --> 00:02:49.940
and it's maybe over.

60
00:02:49.940 --> 00:02:51.180
I don't know.

61
00:02:51.180 --> 00:02:53.020
So you wanna approach these kinds of things

62
00:02:53.020 --> 00:02:54.300
very carefully.

63
00:02:54.300 --> 00:02:56.100
You've spent so much time and energy

64
00:02:56.100 --> 00:02:58.500
in developing authentic and organic community

65
00:02:58.620 --> 00:03:00.060
and trust with these students

66
00:03:00.060 --> 00:03:01.780
and openness and honesty

67
00:03:01.780 --> 00:03:05.260
and being able to ask the difficult questions.

68
00:03:05.260 --> 00:03:06.980
Now is one of those times

69
00:03:06.980 --> 00:03:10.020
where the difficult questions are going to start to come.

70
00:03:10.020 --> 00:03:12.020
But it comes to prophecy.

71
00:03:12.020 --> 00:03:14.500
There just may be those kinds of things.

72
00:03:15.620 --> 00:03:18.780
I can't predict what kind of questions your students

73
00:03:18.780 --> 00:03:21.180
may ask, but from my experience,

74
00:03:21.180 --> 00:03:22.980
this is always one of those areas

75
00:03:22.980 --> 00:03:24.620
that just, it pops up.

76
00:03:25.700 --> 00:03:27.180
So if you don't know the answers

77
00:03:27.220 --> 00:03:29.500
or your small group leaders don't know the answers,

78
00:03:29.500 --> 00:03:32.580
write them down, gather together,

79
00:03:33.580 --> 00:03:35.100
get some answers,

80
00:03:35.100 --> 00:03:37.020
bring your students back together

81
00:03:37.020 --> 00:03:40.820
and give them the answers that they're seeking.

82
00:03:40.820 --> 00:03:42.580
So for this week, don't be afraid

83
00:03:42.580 --> 00:03:46.140
to directly address the misconception.

84
00:03:46.140 --> 00:03:48.140
And here's how we've worded it.

85
00:03:48.140 --> 00:03:50.340
It seems to be entirely impossible

86
00:03:50.340 --> 00:03:54.620
for one man to fulfill hundreds of prophecies,

87
00:03:54.660 --> 00:03:57.540
not to mention that the way Jesus fulfilled

88
00:03:57.540 --> 00:04:00.540
Messianic prophecy was very much contrary

89
00:04:00.540 --> 00:04:02.980
to popular Jewish theology.

90
00:04:02.980 --> 00:04:05.380
Jewish leaders were looking for the coming Messiah

91
00:04:05.380 --> 00:04:09.340
to be a political, military and spiritual ruler

92
00:04:09.340 --> 00:04:11.100
that would dethrone foreign rule

93
00:04:11.100 --> 00:04:14.620
and reestablish Israel as a world superpower.

94
00:04:15.980 --> 00:04:20.660
Instead, Jesus unexpectedly established a spiritual kingdom.

95
00:04:20.660 --> 00:04:23.860
It's a worldview shift that has prevented many

96
00:04:23.900 --> 00:04:26.220
from accepting Him as Savior.

97
00:04:27.460 --> 00:04:28.660
Keep that in mind.

98
00:04:28.660 --> 00:04:33.660
This is a completely worldview shift for many.

99
00:04:34.260 --> 00:04:38.060
It was that way for Jews in the first century

100
00:04:38.060 --> 00:04:39.580
and it's that way probably for many

101
00:04:39.580 --> 00:04:41.140
of your students as well.

102
00:04:41.140 --> 00:04:43.140
Don't be afraid to hit the bell.

